---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout activePage="home">
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Developer portfolio</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">A simple place for my work, experiments, and notes.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        I am Amal Jacob, a developer working mainly with React and Java. This site is
        starting small: a clean home base that I can keep improving as I build more
        personal projects and learn in public.
      </p>
      <div class="actions" aria-label="Primary links">
        <a class="button primary" href="/projects/">View projects</a>
        <a class="button" href="/contact/">Contact me</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <aside class="status-card" aria-label="Current focus">
      <h2>Current Focus</h2>
      <ul class="status-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Frontend</strong>
          <span>React interfaces, component structure, accessibility, and practical UI polish.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Backend</strong>
          <span>Java services, APIs, data flow, and production-minded engineering habits.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Personal Work</strong>
          <span>Small experiments, useful tools, and project write-ups as they take shape.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="section-grid" aria-label="Site overview">
    <article class="info-card">
      <p class="card-label">About</p>
      <h2>Who I Am</h2>
      <p>
        A developer building a personal space for work that does not always fit neatly
        into a resume: experiments, notes, rough ideas, and lessons from real projects.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="info-card">
      <p class="card-label">Projects</p>
      <h2>What Will Go Here</h2>
      <p>
        Personal builds, learning projects, prototypes, and small utilities. The first
        entries can start simple and grow into proper write-ups over time.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="info-card">
      <p class="card-label">Contact</p>
      <h2>How To Reach Me</h2>
      <p>
        A direct contact page with an email address and links you choose to make public.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
